# LF in the repository and LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# This is not cosmetic. The test fixtures hold Blutter disassembly copied out
# verbatim as triple-quoted Python strings, and the parser is line-oriented. On
# a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true (the default on GitHub's Windows
# runners) those literals would pick up \r, get written to the fixture file,
# and the parser would be fed input that does not match what Blutter actually
# produces. Pinning eol=lf keeps the Windows CI job testing the same bytes as
# the Linux one.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched by the newline logic.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.so  binary
*.apk binary
*.zip binary
